<title>UK: HFC Bank to pay 14.2 million stg to parent - paper.</title>
<headline>HFC Bank to pay 14.2 million stg to parent - paper.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>HFC Bank, the credit card and loan group will pay 14.2 million stg ($22.95 million) to U.S. parent company Household International, the Financial Times said on Thursday.</p>
<p>The payment is the first HFC has made to its parent since running into bad debt trouble at the end of the 1980s, the FT said.</p>
<p>HFC, which operates British Gas Plc's Goldfish credit card, boosted pre-tax profits by 38 percent to 54.9 million stg last year.</p>
</text>
